      "text": "To determine the type of curve on which all the points \\((x, y) = \\left( \\frac{t + 1}{t}, \\frac{t - 1}{t} \\right)\\) lie, we will express \\(y\\) in terms of \\(x\\) and then analyze the resulting relationship between \\(x\\) and \\(y\\).\n\nGiven:\n\\[ x = \\frac{t + 1}{t} \\]\n\\[ y = \\frac{t - 1}{t} \\]\n\nFirst, we solve for \\(t\\) in terms of \\(x\\):\n\n\\[ x = \\frac{t + 1}{t} \\]\n\\[ x t = t + 1 \\]\n\\[ x t - t = 1 \\]\n\\[ t (x - 1) = 1 \\]\n\\[ t = \\frac{1}{x - 1} \\]\n\nNow, substitute \\( t = \\frac{1}{x - 1} \\) into the equation for \\(y\\):\n\n\\[ y = \\frac{t - 1}{t} \\]\n\\[ y = \\frac{\\frac{1}{x - 1} - 1}{\\frac{1}{x - 1}} \\]\n\\[ y = \\frac{\\frac{1 - (x - 1)}{x - 1}}{\\frac{1}{x - 1}} \\]\n\\[ y = \\frac{1 - x + 1}{1} \\]\n\\[ y = 1 - x \\]\n\nThus, the relationship between \\(x\\) and \\(y\\) is given by the equation:\n\\[ y = 1 - x \\]\n\nThis is the equation of a line in slope-intercept form \\(y = mx + b\\), where \\(m = -1\\) and \\(b = 1\\).\n\nTherefore, all the plotted points lie on a line.\nThe final answer is \\(\\boxed{\\text{A}}\\).",
