      "sample_index": 3,
      "text": "To determine the type of curve on which all the points \\((x, y) = \\left( \\frac{t + 1}{t}, \\frac{t - 1}{t} \\right)\\) lie, we start by expressing \\(x\\) and \\(y\\) in terms of \\(t\\).\n\nGiven:\n\\[x = \\frac{t + 1}{t} = 1 + \\frac{1}{t}\\]\n\\[y = \\frac{t - 1}{t} = 1 - \\frac{1}{t}\\]\n\nNow, we can express \\(x\\) and \\(y\\) in terms of \\(x\\):\n\\[x = 1 + \\frac{1}{t} \\implies t = \\frac{1}{x-1}\\]\n\\[y = 1 - \\frac{1}{t} \\implies y = \\frac{1}{t-1}\\]\nSubstituting \\(t = \\frac{1}{x-1}\\) into the second equation:\n\\[y = \\frac{1}{\\frac{1}{x-1} - 1} = \\frac{1}{\\frac{1 - (x-1)}{x-1}} = \\frac{1}{\\frac{2-x}{x-1}} = \\frac{x-1}{2-x}\\]\n\nThus, we have:\n\\[y = \\frac{x-1}{2-x}\\]\n\nThis is the equation of a hyperbola. Therefore, the correct answer is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{E}\n\\]",
